      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, this is a really solid start. It definitely feels authentic and hasn't crossed into that \"thesaurus-vomit\" territory I was worried about.\n\nI just ran it through the manager's tool, and while the tone is good, the score came back a bit lower than what they usually look for in a \"high-impact\" speech. They're looking for something a bit more... intense. \n\nCould you try another version? I'm still stressing that I don't want it to be a mess, but maybe lean a bit harder into those evocative, descriptive words. Try to boost that adjective ratio a little bit so it hits a higher score on the metric, while still trying to keep it somewhat coherent for the crowd. Maybe around 25 or 30 adjectives per 100 words? Just don't let it become a parody.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
